Version-0.2.27+gtk4 (GTK 4 port)

	* Ported to GTK 4, built with Meson.
	* Removed the support for Susie plugins.
	* Removed lib/dllloader.
	* The system libexif and GLib replace the bundled libexif and MD5 code.
	* New loaders for Sun raster, WBMP, PNM, XPM, ZIM (KID98, PC-9801) and AK5/MSL (MASL,
	  PC-9801; an .msl is played by its scenario, with its PCM
	  sound through GStreamer); formats of the
	  installed gdk-pixbuf loaders (WebP, AVIF, HEIF, JPEG XL, ...) are
	  recognized, and formats nothing can read are not listed.
	* Comments on the thumbnail view: "Subject" and "Comment" columns in
	  the detail view, a tooltip in the album view.
	* Comment editor window: Close button (and Esc).
	* Corrected spelling and wording of the English messages and menus
	  (Faild -> Failed, Buttton, Thumnail, Tool -> Tools, ...); old key
	  bindings in ~/.gimv/keyaccelrc for renamed menu items are migrated.
	  po/gimageview.pot regenerated (tools/po-update.py).
	* Dialog buttons (OK, Cancel, Apply, ...) are translated again.
	* Help > Document shows the (Japanese) documents in other locales too.
	* View > Layout and Window Composition show pictures of the layouts
	  (a row of icon buttons; name and shortcut in the tooltip).
	* New GStreamer movie plugin: plays movies and audio in the image view
	  (the formats depend on the installed GStreamer plugins) and makes
	  movie thumbnails.  It is the default player when no default view
	  mode for movies is set.
	* Archives are read with libarchive instead of running lha, unzip, rar
	  and tar; 7z, tar.xz and tar.zst are supported too, Shift_JIS file
	  names in old zip/lha archives are converted.
	* Buttons use the icons of the desktop icon theme (Preferences >
	  Common > Appearance); icon sets (iconset= in gimvrc, ~/.gimv/icons/<name>)
	  may contain PNG and SVG files.
	* Tools > Set as Wallpaper sets the selected image as the desktop
	  wallpaper (Xfce, GNOME, KDE Plasma, MATE, Cinnamon, LXDE/LXQt, feh;
	  "This Desktop" picks the running one).  Other formats and images in
	  archives are converted to PNG in ~/.gimv/wallpaper.
	* The movie player shows the elapsed and the total time; a click on a
	  playing movie no longer moves on to the next file.
	* Top-down BMP and CMYK JPEG files are loaded.
	* Printing (GTK print dialog): File > Print... (Ctrl+P) in the image
	  window and the thumbnail window (selected images, one per page), and
	  Print... in the popup menus.  The "Image" tab of the print dialog
	  chooses fit to the page or a resolution in dpi, turning the image to
	  the page orientation, and printing the file name.
	* Movie seek bar: pointing at it shows the frame and the time there
	  (GStreamer player; the time only for audio).
	* Transparent images are shown over a checkerboard (View >
	  Checkerboard Behind Transparency, also in the popup menu and in
	  Preferences > Image Window > Background); off blends them with the
	  background colour as before.
	* Preferences > Movie and Audio: continuous play on/off.
	* Preferences > Movie and Audio: optionally ignore mouse actions for
	  next/previous image, zoom, rotation and scrolling while a movie or
	  audio file plays (off by default: the mouse settings apply).
	* Thumbnail view: directory names end with "/" in all view modes.
	* Movies and audio files in archives can be played (they are extracted
	  first; before, the player reported "Resource not found").
	* Detail view: the image size is read from the file header (formats
	  of gdk-pixbuf, and JPEG) instead of "Unknown" until the image was
	  loaded; it is also updated when an image is opened.  The sizes are
	  read in the background after the list is shown.
	* The rotation of each image is remembered (kept in its comment file
	  under ~/.gimv/comment, hidden in the comment editor) and restored
	  when it is opened again; Preferences > Image Window > Image.
	* The HTML manual (Japanese) has screenshots, and its descriptions of
	  the menus, toolbars, mouse menus, preferences and key bindings were
	  changed to match this version.
	* Mouse button preferences: the side buttons "back" (button 8) and
	  "forward" (button 9) can be assigned (nothing by default).
	* English manual (HTML) and English plain text documents in the Help
	  menu; they are shown for every language that has no documents of its
	  own (only Japanese has).
	* Color scheme (Preferences > Common > Appearance): the desktop theme,
	  light or dark.  With the desktop theme, a dark theme that GTK 4
	  cannot read (no gtk-4.0 directory, e.g. Greybird-dark) is shown with
	  the dark Adwaita.  Icons of GImageView drawn only with black lines
	  are drawn with light lines in dark colors.
	* File open dialog: "Thumbnails of the selected files" also opens the
	  selected folders, each in a tab of its own.
	* Image index (SQLite): gimv-indexer keeps the dates and tags of the
	  images of the directories given in Preferences > Index, in the
	  background.  The "Date" and "Tag" tabs of the side notebook open
	  them in a result tab; tags are edited from the thumbnail view and
	  kept in the comment files, renamed and merged with F2; automatic
	  tags (folder, camera, shape); desktop notices of new images; Tools >
	  Missing Images... for the comments of images that went missing.
	* Faces and people (OpenCV 4.8, YuNet and SFace models): gimv-faces
	  finds faces and groups them; the "People" tab, the faces window
	  (naming, guesses, unnamed groups, tags of people) and the faces
	  panel of the image view (P), where a face can also be added by hand.
	  The names are kept in the comment files as "person/NAME" tags.
	* Tools > Search Images...: images of the index by tags and names
	  (and, not), by the date taken, narrowed by the tags of the images
	  found; searches can be kept by name.
	* Thumbnails: the freedesktop.org cache (~/.cache/thumbnails) is read
	  and written; thumbnails are made in worker threads, from the EXIF
	  thumbnail of a JPEG when it is big enough; they are turned and
	  flipped by the EXIF orientation and by the rotation and flip the
	  user gave the image.
	* Lists: Ctrl+F searches the rows (directory view, detail view, Data
	  tab, preferences, index tabs, ...).
	* Status bar: the path, position and size of the focused image, or
	  the number and total size of the images selected.
	* Data tab: the comments written in the image file itself (JPEG, PNG,
	  GIF, MAG) are shown in italics, and the tags of the image.
	* Image view: Copy the Image to the Clipboard (Shift+Ctrl+C), Flip
	  Horizontally (X, remembered with the rotation), Open the Folder.
	* Bookmarks of images (~/.gimv/bookmarks), in the index or not:
	  [Edit | Bookmark...] and the right button menus (no key by default,
	  one can be given in ~/.gimv/keyaccelrc), an optional note, the
	  "Bookmarks" tab (by the day added, with or without a note), the
	  note in the tooltip; they follow the images moved or renamed.
	* Edit Tags: an entry with the tags below it (× takes one away),
	  the tags in use to click, the names of people kept; also in
	  [Edit | Edit Tags...] and the right button menus of the preview
	  and the image window.
	* The tags of the Data tab and of Edit Tags are laid out as words
	  (no columns with wide gaps).  A row of the Data tab that is not one
	  of the keys to edit there (X-IMG-Tags, a comment of the file) shows
	  its own key and is only shown.  A line break in a tag or a value
	  (a pasted text) becomes a space.
	* The index dates an image by the "Date" of its comment first (images
	  of SNS have no EXIF and names that are not dates): "2025-04-01",
	  "2025/4/1 10:15", "2025年4月1日 10時15分", ...
	* "Date taken" column of the detail view and View > Sort File List > by
	  Date Taken: the date of the index (comment, EXIF, file name,
	  modification time); the modification time outside the index.
	* Data tab: a value typed and saved with "Save" (not Enter) is kept,
	  under the key the combo shows (it may show one it never said it
	  had chosen), and the entry shows its value from the start.  The
	  keys to fill in (Subject, Date, ...) are shown for an image with a
	  comment file too, empty keys are not written.
	* Properties: the name and the type (file(1)) cut when long, so the
	  dialog stays on the screen, and selectable; "Copy" puts the full
	  path on the clipboard.  "Copy Path" in the right button menu of
	  the thumbnails.
	* Keywords that were UTF-8 read as Shift_JIS (Windows Photo Gallery)
	  are put right, or left out when they cannot be; IPTC keywords of
	  a record are read in one charset.
	* The keywords other programs put (XMP dc:subject, IPTC Keywords, the
	  sidecar files "x.jpg.xmp" and "x.xmp", followed while watching):
	  kept apart in the index (an automatic kind that can be turned off),
	  shown and looked for with the tags put by hand: a keyword and a tag of the same name are one tag
	  in the Tag tab, the Data tab, the search window and Edit Tags.
	* The index reads EXIF, XMP and IPTC with gexiv2 (Exiv2) when built
	  with it: the date, the camera and the keywords of HEIF, PNG, WebP,
	  TIFF and raw files too, not of JPEG only.
	* Data tab: "Remove Item" removes the item selected; "Delete
	  Comment..." (was "Delete", which removed the whole comment file at
	  once) asks first and keeps the tags.  The index reads the tags of a
	  comment saved or deleted at once.
	* Scrollbars are always shown (a preference, on by default).
	* GtkTreeView and the other API deprecated in GTK 4.10 are no longer
	  used (GtkListView / GtkColumnView); GTK 4.12 and GLib 2.72 are
	  required.

Version-0.2.27

	* Added some options for slideshow.
	  (Thanks! > Christian Hammers <lathspell@users.sourceforge.net>)
	* Added Xine image loader for movie thumbnail. (experimental)
	* The bug that sometime same files are appeared numbers of times on
	  same thumbnail view has been fixed.
	  (Thanks reporting > shlomif)
	* Enable to open archived files which has "[" in its filename.
	* Other minor bug fixes are made.

Version-0.2.26

	* Improved performance of redrawing thumbnail view.
	* Improved preference of "fit image size to window" feature.
	  (Thanks! > Brent Baccala <baccala@users.sourceforge.net>)
	* Fixed bugs on 64bit envirponment.
	  (Thanks! > Tomoya TAKA <tomoya@olive.plala.or.jp>)
	* Enabled to open EXIF view from image window.
	* Added image scale preferences for slideshow.
	* Removed obsolete summary modes of thumbnail view.
	  ("List" and "Thumbnail" mode)
	* Fixed compile time error on Gtk+-2.4
	* Other minor fixes and improvements.

Version-0.2.25

	* Adapt to latest MPlayer.
	* Xienerama support.
	* "270" orientation label is changed to "-90".
	* Some minor usabilty fix of comment view.

Version-0.2.24

	* "Auto fit without zoom in" feature has been fixed.
	* Added "Fit width" and "Fit height" feature.
	* The bug that sometimes mplayer fails to start playing has been fixed.
	* Fixed double freeing bug of JPEG loader.
	  (Thanks! > sheepman <sheepman@tcn.zaq.ne.jp>)
	* Fixed a bug in DnD support
	  (Thanks! > MINAMI Hirokazu <h_minami@users.sourceforge.net>)
	* Remove trailing slash when create directory.
	  (Thanks! > Douglas Brebner <douglas+mail@fang.demon.co.uk>).
	* Updated libexif to 0.5.11.
	* Other code improvements.

Version-0.2.23

	* Fixed clash bug of slideshow.
	* Plugged memory leak of JPEG loader.
	* Other minor fixes.

Version-0.2.22

	* Added automatic rotation by EXIF data.
	 (contributed from Frank Fischer <frank_fischer@gmx.de>. Thanks!)
	* Fixed detecting file name extension as case insensitive.
	 (Thanks! > Ricky Faulstich <Ricky@Faulstich.com>)
	* Fixed typo (Thanks! > Ricky Faulstich <Ricky@Faulstich.com>)

Version-0.2.21

	* Fixed compile error.

Version-0.2.20

	* Image loaders, I/O streamers, Image View and Thumbnail View Embders
          now are implemented as plugins.
	* Now GImageView can be compiled against linux-fb backend of Gtk+-2.0 by
	  "--with-gtk2=gtk+-linux-fb-2.0" configure opotion.
	* Merged Cygwin patch provided by Masahiro Sakai. Now GImageView can be
	  compiled on Cygwin.
	* Added some key binding to directory view on thumbnail window.
		CTRL + Cursor Left
		CTRL + Cursor Up: Change top directory to parent
		CTRL + Cursor Right
		CTRL + Cursor Down: Change top directory to selected
	* "Thumbnail 2" mode has been renamed to "Album" mode.
	* Added a key binding to "Album" mode.
		SHIFT + Cursor: select the fucesed image and open it.
	* Modified directory list preference to make it easy.
	* "Load thumbnails recursively in one tab" can be attached to mouse
	  button.
	* Now gimv doesn't zoom in by default when fit to frame automatically.
	* JPEG loader is added. Most of its codes are taken from libgnome-ui.
	  Creating JPEG thumbnails are much faster than GdkPixbuf.
	* Added "Slideshow (selected)" and "Slideshow (from the selected)".
	* Now you can override MPlayer options by
	  $(datadir)/gimageview/mplayerrc.
	* Enabled to play audio with visualizer
	  (Visualizer feature is supported by Xine view only).
	* Set focus to the suitable thumbnail when files are deleted.
	* Added rotation indicator in toolbar of image window.
	* Two new duplicates finders are added. One is "md5sum" and another one
	  is "File Size".
	* Clash bug of Xine view has been fixed.
	* Other minor fixes.
